WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.700 --> 00:00:07.401
An order takes three calls: charge the card, reserve the item, and ship it.

2
00:00:07.401 --> 00:00:12.228
If the process dies in between, the card is charged and nothing else happens.

3
00:00:12.433 --> 00:00:16.689
Durable execution keeps this code and makes it survive the crash.

4
00:00:16.689 --> 00:00:19.700
A server keeps an event history for every run.

5
00:00:19.933 --> 00:00:23.649
When worker 1 reaches charge, it doesn't call the bank itself.

6
00:00:23.649 --> 00:00:28.864
The server records that the charge is scheduled, and an activity worker calls the bank.

7
00:00:29.067 --> 00:00:32.544
The result, charge ch_1, goes into the history.

8
00:00:32.544 --> 00:00:34.541
Reserve works the same way.

9
00:00:34.767 --> 00:00:37.251
The workflow then sleeps for 24 hours.

10
00:00:37.251 --> 00:00:41.500
That becomes a timer in the server, so no thread waits for a day.

11
00:00:41.733 --> 00:00:43.506
Now a deploy kills worker 1.

12
00:00:43.506 --> 00:00:48.317
Everything it held in memory is gone, but the history is safe in the server.

13
00:00:48.533 --> 00:00:51.939
A day later the timer fires, and worker 2 gets the task.

14
00:00:51.939 --> 00:00:56.440
It has never seen this order, so it runs the workflow from the first line.

15
00:00:56.667 --> 00:00:59.914
At charge, the history already holds the result.

16
00:00:59.914 --> 00:01:04.040
So it returns ch_1 at once, and the bank is not called again.

17
00:01:04.267 --> 00:01:06.622
Reserve and sleep replay the same way.

18
00:01:06.622 --> 00:01:11.768
This is replay: run the code again, and answer each finished step from the history.

19
00:01:12.000 --> 00:01:16.668
At ship, the history runs out, so this time the activity really runs.

20
00:01:16.668 --> 00:01:19.373
One charge, one reservation, one parcel.

21
00:01:19.600 --> 00:01:20.716
One gap is left.

22
00:01:20.716 --> 00:01:25.599
Suppose the worker charges the card, then dies before it reports back.

23
00:01:25.599 --> 00:01:28.111
The server never records the result.

24
00:01:28.333 --> 00:01:34.440
After a timeout, the server runs the charge again, and the bank charges the card a second time.

25
00:01:34.440 --> 00:01:36.304
Activities run at least once.

26
00:01:36.567 --> 00:01:42.626
Give the charge an idempotency key built from the workflow id: order-42 slash charge.

27
00:01:42.626 --> 00:01:47.545
Every retry sends the same key, so the bank returns the first charge.

28
00:01:47.767 --> 00:01:49.984
The engine records each step once.

29
00:01:49.984 --> 00:01:51.876
The bank still needs the key.
